doc={'openapi':'3.1.0','info':{'title':'SSO Public Platform API','version':'0.20.0','description':'External server/native-client contract. Local reference server only; production requires TLS and configured public origins. OAuth code+S256 PKCE, platform audience https://api.sso.local. No cookie authentication or wildcard CORS; browser integrations use a BFF. All writes require MFA authenticated within 300 seconds; refresh does not update auth_time. Tenant-scoped roles grant separate member/organization/invitation/audit permissions; explicit deny wins. Only active owners manage roles and owner bindings; roles.manage cannot be delegated or denied via custom policies. Resource/subtree scopes are not implemented. Delegated member operators cannot suspend/restore owner bindings. Authorization is checked against the business primary inside each operation transaction. Tenant-version mutations invalidate prior tenant grants, requiring new authorization. JSON objects reject duplicate keys, unknown fields, invalid UTF-8 and extra documents. Only role policy requests admit typed nested rules, with depth/work and policy-count limits. Request body limit 4096 bytes. UUIDs are lowercase 32-hex strings. List limit 1–100, default 50; after is previous next_cursor. No pagination snapshot guarantee. Error format follows RFC 9457. All responses no-store. Invitation proofs never appear in lists/detail/audit; creation and explicit reissue each return only their new one-time proof.'},'servers':[{'url':'http://api.localhost:8083','description':'Local acceptance only; SRE owns production deployment'}],'tags':[{'name':'Identity'},{'name':'Tenant management'}],'paths':paths,'components':{'securitySchemes':{'OAuth2':{'type':'oauth2','flows':{'authorizationCode':{'authorizationUrl':'http://auth.localhost:4464/oauth2/auth','tokenUrl':'http://auth.localhost:4464/oauth2/token','refreshUrl':'http://auth.localhost:4464/oauth2/token','scopes':{'platform:read':'Read identity and authorized space metadata','platform:write':'Modify authorized space resources and own sessions; recent MFA required'}}}}},'schemas':schemas,'parameters':parameters,'responses':responses,'headers':headers}}
for path,contents in [(root/'api/openapi.yaml',yaml.safe_dump(doc,allow_unicode=True,sort_keys=False)),(root/'api/openapi.json',json.dumps(doc,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')]:
 if '--check' in sys.argv:
  if path.read_text()!=contents:raise SystemExit('Public API contract is stale')
 else:path.write_text(contents)
